# Basic photographic development — the controls a raw developer gives you,
# all in one GPU pass.
#
# Deliberately one algorithm rather than ten chained ones. Chained GPU stages
# are bandwidth-bound: at 36 MP each stage reads and writes a 144 MB
# intermediate, so ten of them would move ~2.9 GB and cost roughly half a
# second per slider nudge. Fused, the image is read once and written once and
# every adjustment happens in registers.
#
# Drop a raw file (.CR3, .ARW, .NEF, ...) onto the "test" row to develop it.

src = image("test")

developed = params(basic_adjust)(src)

display(src,       "1 original")
display(developed, "2 developed")
